125	- **The compiled checker judges two functional methods by the Meet Rule for Functional Methods, per providing type, and its overloading memo no longer answers across contexts** (`compile-ladder/rung-overloading-checker/REPORT.md`; rows 556, 557, 477, 561, 562, 568 and 569 fixed). Two functional methods at one self position are valid among the top-level functionals; every type that provides both must provide the meet, except a pair one of whose declarations is the component's own abstract one, which no check reads (row 572): the check reads every declaration in an api, and in a component those with bodies and every one inherited from an api, and compares the meet without the self parameter wherever it sits. An inherited method's static parameters are renamed apart from its trait's; the memo is keyed on the check's inputs; an excludes clause's reciprocal entry is read with its trait's parameters in scope; a character literal is typed by each world's library. An object expression is checked by no per-provider rule, so a pair only it provides goes unchecked (row 570, home 2, behind row 375's code-generation stop). What the rule and the `Character` typing move in the count and the distance (top-level pairs and captured sites gone, pairs per providing type in the apis and the components, errors unmasked) is in REPORT section 10. Gated by `compiler_tests/FunctionalMethodMeetPerProvider`, `FunctionalMethodMeetSelfSecond`, `XXXFunctionalMethodMeetInheritedFromApi`, `GenericTraitExcludesKindEnv`, `InheritedMethodStaticParamSameName`, `InheritedFunctionalMethodStaticParamSameName` and `XXXFunctionalMethodMeetJoinOfClosedTraits`.
