132	FACTS.md:97
133	- **The `XXX` expected-failure mechanism in `compiler_tests/` and `library_tests/` can express a compile-stage failure only, and a run-time defect needs two `.test` files** (`compile-ladder/rung-tryatomic/`). `shouldFail` comes from the `.test` file name (`FileTests.java:1049`) and reaches every stage the file drives (`:1169-1186`), so an `XXX` file that carries `link` or `compile` demands that the compile fail (`:394-414`), while an unsatisfied `run_out_*` verdict fails whatever `shouldFail` says (`:605-610`, `:654-656`; `pass`/`PASS` is the default check, `:276-282`). A compiles-but-crashes defect is therefore two `.test` files over one component, a plain-named one driving `link` and an `XXX`-named one driving `run` with a marker the failing run prints; a refusal is one compile test. Run in one JVM (`junit.sh`'s `ONE_JVM=1`, `compile-ladder/climb-batch-N/merged-tests/junit.sh`), the compile and link tests run before the run tests (`FileTests.java:1114-1121`).
134	
