136	- **An `XXX` compile test pinned by `compile_err_contains` whose program compiles is reported as a wrong failure, not a missing one** (`compile-ladder/rung-unknown-size-arm/probes/pre-edit-tests.txt`). The harness evaluates the check key whether or not the command failed, so a missed key fails with "Saw wrong failure" even when the compile exited 0 (`tests/unit_tests/FileTests.java:394-412`); "Missing expected failure" appears only with no key or a met one. Either way the test is red. A compile that throws is checked on its `exception` key, " OK Saw expected exception" (`:342-366`).
