142	- **The checker-count and distance stages read only the compiler's phases, so an edit to the test corpora, the texts or walk's evaluator and natives cannot move them** (`coordinator/climb-batch-workflow.md`, "Rules weighed by what they cost against what they protect", item 5). Both stages run `Shell.compilerPhases` with `PhaseOrder.compilerPhaseOrder` (`coordinator/tools/checker-count/WorldFlip.java:42`, `coordinator/tools/distance/DistanceMulti.java:64`; `ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/phases/PhaseOrder.java:137-147`, `ENVGEN` not in it), which reads no test, text or record. Outside `interpreter/`, walk's evaluator classes are named only by walk's commands in `Shell.java` (`:607-621`, `:1221`), by `ENVGEN`'s `compiler/environments/`, as field types of the exception classes and in the unused `compiler/codegen/Common.java`, and walk's natives only in the library's strings, which walk resolves. That is by reading, and four runs on an interpreter-only edit agree with it. The batch script acts on it by its `STAGE_BLIND` rule: a rung all of whose paths are under `explorations/`, `Specification/`, `Documentation/`, a test corpus, `interpreter/evaluator/`, `interpreter/glue/` or the test harness (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/tests/`, named outside its package only by `Shell.java`'s `junit` command, `:55` and `:1086`) runs neither stage and says so with the paths, and its skeptic checks the paths against the branch's diff (check 10); the gate measures both on the merged tree either way.
