147	- **The true distance to the switch-over, measured on today's tree: on the flat library the checker reports 1,736 distinct errors under walk's setting and 1,527 under the compile path's, of which the gate's count shows 62** (`perf-probes/prelude/switch-over-distance-flat.md`, scripts and captures under `perf-probes/prelude/switch-over-distance-flat/`; on the nested tower the totals were 2,523 and 2,359, `perf-probes/prelude/switch-over-distance.md`). The title's figures are that measurement's, on an earlier flat library. The last landed gate reads 340 under the gate's setting `any`, the bound `Any` with compiled-expression desugaring (POSITIONS, "The implicit bound of an unbounded type parameter is `Any`"), and a count of 1 (`compile-ladder/climb-batch-9/gate/distance.txt`, `checker-count.txt`, `summary.txt`); walk's setting and the compile path's own `extends Object` setting are not measured by the gate. Over twelve prelude apis and their twelve components, the overloading memo off, in one JVM (`DistanceMulti.java`), the 340 are: exclusion 0; `comprises` 0; overloading 2; return type 2; abstract method not implemented 12; the `extends Object` bound 0; other well-formedness 36; component bodies' type errors 280; export mismatches 8 (`distance.txt:3-11`; by root cause in the next entry). Each landed batch's movement by kind, unit and class is in its gate's `summary.txt`, its `distance` lines, and in its record's last section ("The landing" or "The gate"), under `compile-ladder/climb-batch-*/`. Three declarations crash the checker, `__bigOperator`'s local function ("Type is not inferred") and the untyped `fn` parameters in the rank-2 and rank-3 array traits, and so does `Stream`'s variance stage (`distance.txt:43-46`): four crash rows. Code generation, measured once by the title's measurement: `FortressLibrary` emits 326 declarations and refuses 225, 4 of them on declarations the checker passed; the overload rewriting's `BottomType` stop is gone; the dispatch generator finishes and refuses 12 of 198 overload sets (131 of 283 on the nested tower). The count stage runs walk's setting (by reading its code) and sees 1 of the distance's 340; its per-api rows count each error twice (`FortressLibrary` 2 against the total 1). The count stage runs the `FortressLibrary` api's overloading and return-type checks, which `StaticChecker` skips while a unit has an earlier error (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/StaticChecker.java:268-272`); the api's last early error, `AnyIntegral`'s `comprises` clause, is cleared ("The tower closure of `02d09a39f` has no spelling the compiler's checker accepts" below). Those checks add 1 error, the overloading of `isLeftZero` in `LexicographicReduction` (`compile-ladder/gate/distance-sites.tsv`), counted twice and already counted by the distance stage. A zero count is necessary, not sufficient (`coordinator/library-route-judgement.md:33`). As a gate stage the one JVM matches the twelve separate runs within the variation; it is reported and never red, and compares with the last landed table (`last_landed_distance`, the gate's step 9, in `gateRole` of `coordinator/climb-batch-workflow.js`); each landed batch's table is in its own gate directory, climb batch 7C's and N's in upper case. Its per-site list lands at one fixed path, `compile-ladder/gate/distance-sites.tsv`, overwritten at each landing (the commit stage's step 1), so that a rung whose test is this stage takes the landed tables as its before (POSITIONS, "No re-measuring what the record holds"); the batches landed before that practice have theirs beside their tables as `gate/distance-sites.tsv`. A run takes 786 to 1,212 s at a gate beside the other stages (each gate's `#seconds` row), 1,130 s under a load of 5.4 with `testFast` and a review beside it (`FortressLibrary` 784 s of it), and 14 to 24 minutes on a shared machine at load 7 to 18 (4 CPUs, Xeon 2.10 GHz, the 1,212 s at 2.80 GHz, JDK 25.0.4, `FORTRESS_THREADS=1`). Runs vary by 2 to 4 errors, in big operators' bodies typed at their element and in the type a join infers for an array body (`compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/probes/distance-variation-base.txt`, `distance-variation-post.txt`, `compile-ladder/rung-tabulate/probes/distance-base-variation.txt`); repeated runs of one setup are identical site for site, and the varying families BR, V2 and O1 move between setups (the entry on the written bound `Object` below) and under edits that touch none of their declarations. Two such moves are attributed: the `comprises` rule's subtype queries in the hierarchy pass add the BR error at `Library/FortressLibrary.fss:1535` and respell or move three other body-check sites, the same in five runs of that build and absent under the broad form of the rule, which clears the same two H2 errors without the queries (`compile-ladder/rung-comprises-checker/probes/skeptic/distance-attribution.txt`); and the integer `MIN`/`MAX` declarations moved the family, touching none of its declarations, one BR site (`BIG MAXNUM`'s body) gone and `BIG //`'s body and a second error in `BIG SQCAP`'s body new, each message on file in distance tables before the edit (`compile-ladder/rung-integer-minmax/REPORT.md` section 8). The candidate cause, the trait table's memos keyed by `TraitType`, is ruled out: with them off the stage gives the same errors site for site (`reviews/row-488-probe.md`; "`TypeAnalyzer.parents` and `excludesClause` are memoized per trait table" below). The mechanism is not known (row 488, open).
